      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T23:06:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general, PortableTypeface should only be used in gms and when the text is a label (not logically part of the gm image under test). It can also be used if the intent really is to use the portable typefaces as a way to test something very specific (we don\u0027t think we would get code coverage testing with any native fonts), but this is pretty rare.\n\nIn general, I find it too easy to slap \"PortableFont\" onto things to try to make them more deterministic instead of getting real coverage and fixing issues. The reality is that no one sees any of those portable fonts but Skia developers, but a few billion people a day are looking at some of the default system fonts.\n\nI\u0027m sure I haven\u0027t quite reviewed all the uses here yet, will take another look later. Also, while Skia has pretty good test coverage, the organic way that coverage has grown turns into a lot of tests which don\u0027t seem to be covering much, but might be the one that covers some odd case, so it\u0027s really difficult to clean them up.",
      "revId": "3608744d4b3cd66e7ec9b6903addfea5f90bbe55",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
