      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T23:06:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`DefaultFont`? There\u0027s no real point in running this on just the portable font, as we control that to death and then this test isn\u0027t really as interesting.\n\nAlso, this test is structured very oddly. Really we want the output from this original base font, the output from the custom typeface created from it, then the output from the typeface after serializing and deserializing. I suppose this test skipped the middle one. But it is awkward that `make_tf` and its caller need to know about how to pick the original font. I would be a lot easier to follow if the caller picked the typeface and passed that in here, then used it later in the first call to `waterfall`. Then this would be much easier to follow.\n\nThat being said, it should be `DefaultFont` so we get some coverage of real non-sanitized paths from the system fonts.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 48
